# TDD vs Debugging Protocol

Clear distinction between TDD protocol (development) and Debugging protocol (error fixing) - when to use each and how they differ.

## When to Apply

Apply this rule when:
- Implementing, creating, adding, or writing new code
- Fixing errors, bugs, or debugging issues
- Handling development-time errors (build, type, lint, test)
- Handling post-development errors (production, runtime, integration)
- Need to understand when to use TDD vs debugging

