## Common Scenarios

### Scenario 1: New Feature Development

**Problem:** Need to implement new feature.

**Solution:** Use TDD Protocol - Seed ∘ Pro ∘ Pro ∘ Ortho ∘ Latch ∘ Meta

### Scenario 2: Production Bug

**Problem:** Bug reported in production.

**Solution:** Use Debugging Protocol - Retro ∘ Ana ∘ Crux ∘ Ortho ∘ Pro ∘ Latch

### Scenario 3: Development-Time Error

**Problem:** Type error during development.

**Solution:** Quick fix - Retro ∘ Ortho ∘ Pro, then continue TDD

## Exceptions

- Skip TDD for trivial code (getters, simple utilities)
- Skip full debugging for obvious errors (typos, syntax)

## Checklist

**For TDD:**
- [ ] Test written from first principles
- [ ] Test fails for right reason
- [ ] Minimal code to pass
- [ ] Refactored if needed
- [ ] Tests pass and comprehensive

**For Debugging:**
- [ ] Error reproduced
- [ ] Root cause identified
- [ ] Fix applied (not just symptom)
- [ ] Verification complete
- [ ] Regression test added

